.TH "getTimeMap" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
getTimeMap \- get the logical time and the corresponding system time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]stp.getTimeMap()\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Stp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to get the logical time and system time of the STP node.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
None
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return an object of type
BSONObj.
Users can get the logical time and the corresponding system time through this
object.
For field descriptions is as follows:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l l l.
T{
0
T}@T{
Name
T}@T{
Type
T}@T{
Description
T}
_
T{
1
T}@T{
TimeMap.LogicalTime
T}@T{
number
T}@T{
Logical time in
T}
T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
microseconds.
T}
T{
2
T}@T{
TimeMap.RealTime
T}@T{
timestamp
T}@T{
System time in
T}
T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
microseconds.
T}
.TE
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v5.0.4 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Get the logical time and system time of the STP node.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> var stp = new Stp()
> stp.getTimeMap()
{
  "TimeMap": [
    {
      "LogicalTime": 1679767981830566,
      "RealTime": {
        "$timestamp": "2023\-03\-24\-04.53.47.000610"
      }
    },
    {
      "LogicalTime": 1679707861320036,
      "RealTime": {
        "$timestamp": "2023\-03\-24\-04.51.01.000039"
      }
    }
  ]
}
\f[]
